<template>
    <heading>SelectProject async work</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>SelectProject</li>
        <li>async</li>
        <li>directory picker</li>
        <li>completion command</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Selection involves asynchronous work, but command legality must remain with the HSM. This function reports completion rather than holding the state handler inside an <code>await</code>. A local picker must be invoked before the first suspension so the Select click's user activation reaches the browser API; remote selection needs no picker.</p>
        <p>Dismissing the picker is an expected user decision, represented by <code>ProjectPickerAborted</code>. Only the picker call has that interpretation: an <code>AbortError</code> from persistence or loading is still a failure. Other errors escape to fatal reporting because recovery has not been defined.</p>
        <p>The <code>ProjectLoaded</code> controller command lets the HSM complete selection; it is separate from the model event of the same name, which informs data observers. Both mean the entire model is available, not merely that a directory was chosen. Local handle persistence precedes model selection and loading; remote projects use the directory-name convention for their root filename. Completion uses deferred dispatch so even a prompt picker dismissal cannot reach the state generator while its entry code is running.</p>
        <p>Reload reuses the model's selected storage object and calls <code>loadProject()</code> without opening a picker or changing selection. It reports the same completion command so the HSM returns to its normal command handler.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>SelectProject async work</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
async function asyncSelectProject(selection) {
    let project;
    if (selection.location === "remote") {
        project = storage.remote.open(selection.url);
    } else {
        let directoryHandle;
        try {
            directoryHandle = await window.showDirectoryPicker();
        } catch (error) {
            if (error.name !== "AbortError") throw error;
            controller.dispatch({ name: "ProjectPickerAborted", error });
            return;
        }
        project = storage.local.open(directoryHandle);
        await util.indexedDB.addHandle(directoryHandle);
    }

    await model.selectProject(project);
    await model.loadProject();
    controller.dispatch({ name: "ProjectLoaded" });
}

async function asyncReloadProject() {
    await model.loadProject();
    controller.dispatch({ name: "ProjectLoaded" });
}
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
